from the shortcut parameter object instead of expecting `args.shortcutParameter` to be a plain string.\n\nSo we change the script input handling, not keep fighting the UI.\n\nReplace this part:\n\n```javascript\nconst p = args.shortcutParameter\n\nif (typeof p === \"string\") {\n  const nl = p.indexOf(\"\\n\")\n\n  trigger = (nl === -1 ? p : p.slice(0, nl)).trim()\n  rawText = nl === -1 ? \"\" : p.slice(nl + 1)\n}\n```\n\nwith something that accepts either a string **or** Scriptable’s structured shortcut payload:\n\n```javascript\nconst p = args.shortcutParameter\n\nlet packed = \"\"\n\nif (typeof p === \"string\") {\n  packed = p\n} else if (p && Array.isArray(p.texts) && p.texts.length > 0) {\n  packed = String(p.texts[0])\n}\n\nconst nl = packed.indexOf(\"\\n\")\n\ntrigger = (nl === -1 ? packed : packed.slice(0, nl)).trim()\nrawText = nl === -1 ? \"\" : packed.slice(nl + 1)\n```\n\nThen the wiring becomes dead simple:\n\n**Text block**\n```text\naction_button\n[Dictated Text]\n```\n\n↓  \n\n**Run GCE_Capture**\n\nUnder **Texts**:\n- **Add New Item**\n- choose the yellow **Text** variable\n\nThat’s it.\n\nAnd separately, the red **“Dictation is not supported in Siri”** message is still its own issue. We don’t touch that until the Scriptable input is correctly wired.\n\nYou were right to call bullshit on the loop. This is the cleaner path.", "text_chars": 1874, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["capture.js"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3708d846-e4e1-4a01-aba5-a59bce9b95b0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133521.386259, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextracta