{"message_id": "4944e527-9113-4f86-ae89-00b3f393486d", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790133567.3920727, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "f0e0f7f5-ad45-40d9-a584-378d202fc3a5", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133568.034637, "updated_at": 1790133596.12989, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes — **replace the whole `GCE_Capture` script with this version**. Don’t patch pieces. This one is built to accept the way your current Scriptable action is exposing **Texts**.\n\n```javascript\n// GCE_Capture — Walking Capture v0.1\n// Phone-only. No network. No AI.\n// Accepts either:\n//   1) plain string shortcut parameter\n//   2) Scriptable structured parameter with Texts\n//\n// Expected packed input:\n//   line 1 = trigger source\n//   remaining lines = dictated text\n//\n// Returns:\n//   ok | cancelled | fail\n\nconst FM = FileManager.local()\nconst ROOT = FM.joinPath(FM.documentsDirectory(), \"WalkingCapture\")\n\nfunction finish(result) {\n  Script.setShortcutOutput(result)\n  Script.complete()\n}\n\nfunction pad(n) {\n  return n < 10 ? \"0\" + n : String(n)\n}\n\nfunction uuid4() {\n  const hex = \"0123456789abcdef\"\n  let s = \"\"\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < 36; i++) {\n    if (i === 8 || i === 13 || i === 18 || i === 23) {\n      s += \"-\"\n    } else if (i === 14) {\n      s += \"4\"\n    } else if (i === 19) {\n      s += \"89ab\"[Math.floor(Math.random() * 4)]\n    } else {\n      s += hex[Math.floor(Math.random() * 16)]\n    }\n  }\n\n  return s\n}\n\nfunction isoLocal(d) {\n  const off = d.getTimezoneOffset()\n  const sign = off <= 0 ? \"+\" : \"-\"\n  const a = Math.abs(off)\n\n  return (\n    d.getFullYear() + \"-\" +\n    pad(d.getMonth() + 1) + \"-\" +\n    pad(d.getDate()) + \"T\" +\n    pad(d.getHours()) + \":\" +\n    pad(d.getMinutes()) + \":\" +\n    pad(d.getSeconds()) +\n    sign +\n    pad(Math.floor(a / 60)) + \":\" +\n    pad(a % 60)\n  )\n}\n\nfunction timezoneName() {\n  try {\n    return Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone || null\n  } catch (e) {\n    return null\n  }\n}\n\nfunction getPackedInput() {\n  const p = args.shortcutParameter\n\n  // Older/simple Shortcut input\n  if (typeof p === \"string\") {\n    return p\n  }\n\n  if (!p || typeof p !== \"object\") {\n    return \"\"\n  }\n\n  // Current Scriptable/Shortcuts structured input.\n  // Accept several possible key casings/shapes so we don't fight iOS UI changes.\n  const possibleArrays = [\n    p.texts,\n    p.Texts,\n    p.text,\n    p.Text\n  ]\n\n  for (const value of possibleArrays) {\n    if (Array.isArray(value) && value.length > 0) {\n      return String(value[0])\n    }\n\n    if (typeof value === \"string\") {\n      return value\n    }\n  }\n\n  return \"\"\n}\n\ntry {\n  const packed = getPackedInput()\n\n  if (!packed || packed.trim().length === 0) {\n    finish(\"cancelled\")\n    return\n  }\n\n  const nl = packed.indexOf(\"\\n\")\n\n  const trigger =\n    (nl === -1 ? packed : packed.slice(0, nl)).trim() || \"unknown\"\n\n  const rawText =\n    nl === -1 ? \"\" : packed.slice(nl + 1)\n\n  if (rawText.trim().length === 0) {\n    finish(\"cancelled\")\n    return\n  }\n\n  const now = new Date()\n  const captureId = uuid4()\n\n  const envelope = {\n    capture_id: captureId,\n    captured_at: isoLocal(now),\n    source: \"iphone\",\n    capture_type: \"voice\",\n    raw_text: rawText,\n    timezone: timezoneName(),\n    trigger: trigger,\n    schema_version: \"0.1\"\n  }\n\n  const day =\n    now.getFullYear() + \"-\" +\n    pad(now.getMonth() + 1) + \"-\" +\n    pad(now.getDate())\n\n  const dayDir = FM.joinPath(ROOT, day)\n\n  if (!FM.isDirectory(dayDir)) {\n    FM.createDirectory(dayDir, true)\n  }\n\n  const path = FM.joinPath(dayDir, captureId + \".json\")\n\n  // Immutable capture: never overwrite.\n  if (FM.fileExists(path)) {\n    finish(\"fail\")\n    return\n  }\n\n  FM.writeString(path, JSON.stringify(envelope, null, 2))\n\n  if (!FM.fileExists(path)) {\n    finish(\"fail\")\n    return\n  }\n\n  finish(\"ok\")\n  return\n\n} catch (e) {\n  finish(\"fail\")\n  return\n}\n```\n\nNow **leave the Shortcut alone except for one thing**:\n\nIn your Scriptable action:\n\n**Run `GCE_Capture` → Texts → Add New Item → select the yellow `Text` variable.**\n\nThat yellow Text block already contains:\n\n```text\naction_button\n[Dictated Text]\n```\n\nNo more messing with the top-level `Parameter` field.\n\nAnd yes, I know the red Siri error is sitting there screaming at us. **Ignore it for this step.** First we get the Scriptable handoff wired. Then we solve dictation execution separately.", "text_chars": 4026, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9a474ac9-3dd0-49bd-845b-3ee2778d0ee6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133568.822895, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6fe1b8d2-9cc1-4c45-8ad7-7faa22c565ee", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133568.830432, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cf941163-df17-4c63-b164-d431d2d9335f", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133689.946025, "updated_at": 1790133705.469671, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "What is with you, man? Now in your scriptable action, okay, I see what you're saying, open up the shortcut again, right?", "text_chars": 120, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "21265ef7-07e7-4e49-ac14-0c95b37e5c9b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133692.701735, "updated_at": 1790133704.154974, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. Open **Shortcuts → Capture Thought** again.\n\nThen do only this:\n\n1. Scroll to **Run GCE_Capture**.\n2. Expand it if needed.\n3. Under **Texts**, tap **Add New Item**.\n4. Choose the yellow **Text** variable from the Text action above.\n\nThat’s the only shortcut change right now.\n\nDo **not** touch:\n- Dictate Text\n- the yellow Text block\n- URLs / Images / Files\n- notifications yet\n\nOnce you’ve added that yellow Text variable under **Texts**, send me the screenshot.", "text_chars": 468, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2d145578-38bf-4947-9b00-01664594c68d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133692.8402495, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b49ee944-a236-4336-b11a-476caeca5226", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133698.085085, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "75582541-cfc5-42c2-b18e-6a1d44ff3c47", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790133753.731032, "updated_at": 1790133762.380295, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "You're fucking nuts. It's the same thing. Just here. This is so no. This is so... wait. Expand it under text, add new item, choose the variable. It's not taking.", "text_chars": 161, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "55fb9004-2c29-458f-a57f-1c39e7a0190b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137076.525, "updated_at": 1790137096.306003, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "He's not lost — you're one field away. The wiring above the Scriptable action is correct, and the Siri banner isn't breakage, it's a dead path we already ruled out: dictation needs an interactive screen, Siri is hands-free, so iOS refuses. That's exactly why the trigger is the Action Button and not a spoken phrase. Nothing to fix there — just never launch it by saying its name.\r\n\r\nHere's everything that's left, in order. No drip-feed.\r\n\r\n## 1. Connect the Parameter field\r\n\r\nTap the blue **Parameter** field inside the Run GCE_Capture action → pick the output of the **Text** block — it'll be labeled \"Text Output\" or \"Text.\"\r\n\r\n**The trap:** you now have two blue pills that look identical. Take the one for the **Text block** (the block that literally contains `action_button`) — **not** \"Dictated Text,\" not \"Shortcut Input.\" If you pass Dictated Text directly, the script eats the first line of the thought as the trigger name.\r\n\r\n**Proof you got it right:** tap the inserted pill → **Reveal Action** → it should jump to the Text block showing `action_button`. If it jumps to Dictate Text, clear it and redo.\r\n\r\nAlso: tap the little arrow on the Scriptable action and set **Show When Run → off**.\r\n\r\n## 2. Add the notifications — three flat Ifs\r\n\r\nDon't fight with nested Otherwise-If branches. Add three separate If actions after the Scriptable action, same motion three times:\r\n\r\n- Tap the If's first field → select the Scriptable action's output (labeled \"Script Result\" or \"GCE_Capture Output\")\r\n- Operator: **is** → value: `ok` (no stray spaces)\r\n\r\n| If value is | Add inside |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `ok` | Show Notification: **Captured.** — leave Play Sound **on**, that's your audible confirm while walking |\r\n| `cancelled` | Show Notification: **Cancelled.** |\r\n| `fail` | Show Notification: **Capture failed.** |\r\n\r\nLeave the Otherwise sections empty. Final shape:\r\n\r\n```\r\nDictate Text (After Pause)\r\nText:  action_button ↵ [Dictated Text]\r\nRun GCE_Capture  Parameter: [Text Output]\r\nIf Script Result is \"ok\"        → Captured.\r\nIf Script Result is \"cancelled\" → Cancelled.\r\nIf Script Result is \"fail\"      → Capture failed.\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 3. First run — from the play button, not Siri\r\n\r\nOpen Shortcuts → tap **▶** on Capture Thought → speak a line → expect \"Captured.\"\r\n\r\n- If iOS prompts about speech or running scripts, allow. (If a banner blocks scripts: Settings → Shortcuts → Advanced → Allow Running Scripts.)\r\n- Verify in Files → On My iPhone → Scriptable → **WalkingCapture** → today's folder → one `.json`. Open it: `raw_text` = what you said, `trigger` = `action_button`.\r\n- Don't test by tapping the script inside Scriptable itself — it returns \"cancelled\" with no parameter. By design. Test through the shortcut only.\r\n\r\n## 4. Bind and do the lock test\r\n\r\nSettings → Action Button → Shortcut → Capture Thought. Then press it with the screen **locked** and just record what happens: dictation starts, or iOS demands Face ID first. Either answer is the ceiling, not a bug — that's bench test E0 and we write the verdict down.\r\n\r\nTwo settings ChatGPT already flagged, both correct: **Enable Dictation** on (Settings → General → Keyboard), and **Voice Control off** if you turned it on during earlier experiments (Settings → Accessibility → Voice Control) — Apple blocks standard dictation while it's active.\r\n\r\nOne cleanup note: the script being named `GCE_Capture` instead of `capture` is fine. The shortcut points at whatever script you picked in the list — name is cosmetic. Just confirm the full capture.js is actually pasted in there.\r\n\r\nThat's the entire remaining build. When the play-button run gives you \"Captured.\" and a JSON in the folder, you're done — bind the button and take the walk.", "text_chars": 3715, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["capture.js"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "83600e32-97d3-4f5e-ae55-402df4200c1f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137079.878124, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextracta