 force that yellow Text variable into the nested **Texts** section.\n\nUse the **top-level blue `Parameter` pill** on the `Run GCE_Capture` action and bind that directly to the output of the yellow **Text** block.\n\nThe exact target is:\n\n**Dictate Text**  \n→ **Text** containing:\n\n```text\naction_button\n[Dictated Text]\n```\n\n→ **Run GCE_Capture with [Text Output]**\n\nAnd the proof is exactly what that pasted guidance says:\n\n- tap the inserted parameter variable\n- choose **Reveal Action**\n- it must jump to the yellow **Text** block containing `action_button`\n- if it jumps to **Dictate Text**, wrong variable\n- if it jumps to **Shortcut Input**, wrong variable\n\nAlso set **Show When Run = off**.\n\nAnd yes: leave the red **“Dictation is not supported in Siri”** banner alone. That’s not the wiring problem. We already decided this shortcut is meant to be launched interactively, especially from the **Action Button**, not by saying its name to Siri.\n\nSo the entire remaining wiring is just:\n\n```text\nDictate Text\n↓\nText: action_button + Dictated Text\n↓\nRun GCE_Capture\n   Parameter = Text Output\n```\n\nNo more expanding **Texts / URLs / Images / Files**. That was the wrong rabbit hole.", "text_chars": 1462, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "05a1954b-cf63-48f8-b662-8b8bcc3f2fa5", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137087.8009, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "026302c9-38da-4a65-b2b3-31ab2aca05ff", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137087.848593, "upda