rameter selector**, not like a normal Shortcuts magic-variable slot.\n\nAnd I checked Scriptable’s own docs: shortcut text passed into a script is exposed through **`args.plainTexts`** when text is supplied by the shortcut action, while `args.shortcutParameter` is a separate generic parameter mechanism that can be text, list, dictionary, or file. citeturn731061search0\n\nSo the clean move is:\n\n**Do not use that blue Parameter field at all.**\n\nUse the expanded section we already see:\n\n**Texts → Add New Item → feed it the yellow Text block output**\n\nThen the script should read from:\n\n```javascript\nargs.plainTexts[0]\n```\n\n—not `args.shortcutParameter`.\n\nThat matches the UI you actually have.\n\nSo the architecture becomes:\n\n```text\nDictate Text\n↓\nText block:\naction_button\n[Dictated Text]\n↓\nRun GCE_Capture\n\nTexts:\n  [yellow Text output]\n\nParameter:\n  LEAVE EMPTY\n```\n\nAnd I should rewrite the full script one more time around **`args.plainTexts` only**, so we stop trying to support three different input paths at once.\n\nIf you want, I’ll give you that final stripped script now — no compatibility junk, just the exact path your phone is showing.", "text_chars": 1397, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "dbd68033-e5d8-48c4-ac25-4e9e98484209", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137299.103689, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "f1cd04bb-51bb-4ea4-963e-61dd4252d9c1", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137299.108344, "updated_at": null, "status": "