, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep. We went down that road already, and the fix is: **stop trying to pass the yellow Text block at all.**\n\nUse the Scriptable action’s **Texts** section as the payload directly.\n\nUnder **Run GCE_Capture → Texts**:\n\n1. Tap **Add New Item**\n2. First text item: type exactly  \n   `action_button`\n3. Tap **Add New Item** again\n4. Second text item: insert the **Dictated Text** variable directly from the Dictate Text action\n\nSo the Scriptable action gets two text inputs:\n\n```text\nTexts:\n  1. action_button\n  2. [Dictated Text]\n```\n\nThen we make the script read:\n\n```javascript\nconst trigger = args.plainTexts[0]\nconst rawText = args.plainTexts[1]\n```\n\nThat completely removes the stupid middle **Text block** and avoids the parameter/file picker mess.\n\nSo yes: **delete the yellow Text action entirely** once we wire those two Text items.\n\nThe shortcut becomes:\n\n```text\nDictate Text\n↓\nRun GCE_Capture\n  Texts:\n    action_button\n    [Dictated Text]\n```\n\nThat is much cleaner. And this time we are using the UI you actually have in front of you, not trying to force a generic “Parameter” workflow onto it.", "text_chars": 1102, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "98be9ea4-2792-4674-8381-74b89ff9a0e1", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137341.98519, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "543b9436-45c2-4f09-80b8-f9137ab0a607", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137342.075009, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "56a17d90-6e49-43d7-a822-db2b6e8499b8", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137415.807112, "updated_at": 1790137427.165553, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Again, how would a parameter when I say add new item text? Nothing saves the text. I'll try it again. Jesus fucking Christ.", "text_chars": 123, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "47e5c137-8e80-4564-8d81-ffcb8171992a", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137417.242738, "updated_at": 1790137426.016771, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah — don’t keep fighting it blindly.\n\nUnder **Texts → Add New Item**, type exactly:\n\n```text\naction_button\n```\n\nThen **do not tap somewhere random**. Use whatever commit control iOS gives you there — usually **Return/Done** on the keyboard. If the field disappears or the text vanishes again, **stop right there and send me that screen**.\n\nBecause if Scriptable’s `Add New Item` UI is not persisting literal text on your phone, then this whole **Texts** route is dead too, and we’ll stop wasting time on it instead of pretending it should work.", "text_chars": 546, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "ee78a9ed-d1e8-42fc-bac1-80aaeb736f53", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137421.248579, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "6d38b2f4-cd3b-40b4-bcb8-03e7849c6f44", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137487.5777512, "updated_at": 1790137497.749931, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer", "text"], "text": "That doesn't save, buddy. Right? I can't enter text. The text is just basically a pass-through.", "text_chars": 95, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["image_asset_pointer"]}, {"message_id": "d415c448-405c-42f0-93df-f7df2904b7b2", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137488.772813, "updated_at": 1790137496.981207, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Exactly. **That screenshot confirms it.**\n\nThe `Texts → Text` row is not a normal editable text field. It’s effectively a **pass-through input slot** for Shortcuts content. That’s why what you type doesn’t persist there.\n\nAnd the toast at the top — **“Capture Failed: No dictated text received.”** — confirms the script is running, but Scriptable is receiving **nothing** in that input channel.\n\nSo the correct conclusion is:\n\n**We stop trying to type literal content into Scriptable’s Texts section.**\n\nThe next thing to test is much narrower:\n\n- Keep `Dictate Text`\n- Remove the yellow Text composition block entirely\n- In Scriptable’s **Texts** section, insert the **Dictated Text magic variable directly** into that pass-through slot\n\nThen simplify the script so it does **not** expect `action_button` to come from the shortcut at all. We can hard-code:\n\n```javascript\nconst trigger = \"action_button\"\nconst rawText = args.plainTexts?.[0] ?? \"\"\n```\n\nThat is cleaner anyway. The shortcut only needs to pass the actual dictated text. The script already knows what triggered it.\n\nSo the new minimal path is:\n\n```text\nDictate Text\n↓\nRun GCE_Capture\n  Texts:\n    [Dictated Text]\n```\n\nNo yellow Text block. No `Parameter`. No typed `action_button` in the Shortcut.\n\nThat removes the exact UI problem you just proved.", "text_chars": 1313, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "67064352-b992-42c1-b61c-de9928c54cf1", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137513.914793, "updated_at": 1790137534.092701, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Okay, but it didn't capture any text. I just ran it.", "text_chars": 52, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "2cb7898c-4152-45a4-afab-29e1426d6512", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137514.779588, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "web.run", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "372b82b4-cb90-4558-84e7-67c4f488977b", "role": "tool", "role_name": "web.run", "created_at": 1790137520.4823463, 