xt": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": ["text"]}, {"message_id": "898e539a-9cea-4be4-8910-6ec33ed1b8a6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790137524.663317, "updated_at": 1790137533.414124, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Right — then **the script is still receiving zero text**. We should stop changing the script blindly.\n\nScriptable’s own docs say `args.plainTexts` is where plain text supplied by a Shortcut action appears. citeturn842607search0 So the next step is to prove whether the Shortcut is actually passing anything into Scriptable.\n\nReplace `GCE_Capture` temporarily with this tiny diagnostic script:\n\n```javascript\nconst result = {\n  plainTexts: args.plainTexts,\n  shortcutParameter: args.shortcutParameter\n}\n\nconst text = JSON.stringify(result, null, 2)\n\nQuickLook.present(text)\nScript.setShortcutOutput(text)\nScript.complete()\n```\n\nThen run **Capture Thought** once and dictate something simple like:\n\n```text\ntest one two three\n```\n\nWhat we want to see is something like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"plainTexts\": [\n    \"test one two three\"\n  ],\n  \"shortcutParameter\": null\n}\n```\n\nIf `plainTexts` is empty, then we know with certainty the failure is **inside the Shortcut wiring**, not in our capture code.\n\nIf the dictated sentence appears there, then the transport works and I’ll give you the final capture script using exactly that proven input path.\n\n**Don’t change anything else yet. Run this probe once and show me what it displays.**", "text_chars": 1224, "code_blocks": 3, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a98b07dd-9af4-46a5-bbdc-ea0736ac712f", 